docs {
  # Alerts Utility Service Tests
  
  Tests for the SIF 3.7 Alerts Utility Service endpoints.
  
  ## What Are Alerts?
  
  Alerts are a system-wide, immutable log of errors, warnings, and status changes.
  Any authenticated environment can create alerts. Query access is ownership-scoped
  (non-admins see only their own alerts, admins see all). Update and Delete are
  prohibited per the SIF 3.7 specification.
  
  ## URL Pattern
  
  Alert endpoints are scoped to a domain and solution:
  - `POST /{domainId}/{solutionId}/alerts/alert` — Create an alert
  - `GET /{domainId}/{solutionId}/alerts` — List alerts
  - `GET /{domainId}/{solutionId}/alerts/{id}` — Get alert by ID
  - `PUT /{domainId}/{solutionId}/alerts/{id}` — Rejected (405)
  - `DELETE /{domainId}/{solutionId}/alerts/{id}` — Rejected (405)
  
  ## Tests Included
  
  - Create alert with messageID
  - Create alert without messageID
  - Create alert with invalid messageID
  - List alerts
  - Get alert by ID
  - Update alert rejected (405)
  - Delete alert rejected (405)
  
  ## Prerequisites
  
  - A domain and solution must exist (createdDomainId, createdSolutionId)
  - An alerts provider must be registered in the environment-global zone
  - Valid authentication credentials
  
  ## Important Notes
  
  - Alerts are immutable: PUT and DELETE return 405
  - Response payloads include SIF_ExtendedElements with server-populated fields
  - Non-admin consumers see only their own alerts
}
